# tests/litscan/spanarms.rxt -- span arms unit E1 ([REQ-EMPTYCAT]'s quantified
# half; docs/design/span_arms.md §4, T2 row 1 in §6): A REPEAT OF A WIDTH-0 BODY
# IS CAT'S UNIT. The necessary run joins the bytes on its two sides
# (src/facts/req.c `rb_rep_rows`), so `abcd(?:\b)*efgh` states `abcdefgh`
# where it stated `efgh`. Every expectation is libpcre2-8 10.46's
# (tests/lib/p2probe.c, lane sae1, 2026-11-09), never pcrec's. Each block
# runs on the default route and again under `engine vm`: the run pre-check
# is emitted into both engines' search entries. W-R4 and S-g are the unit's
# two sabotage witnesses (rows S1906, S1905); a sabotaged run is absent from
# the subject, clears the 16-bit floor, and is pinned by no k-set walk, so
# the pre-check answers NOMATCH where libpcre2 matches.
# Unit R1 ([REPEAT-RUN], T2 rows 2-3, §3) adds the power arm's witnesses: a
# repeat of a consuming body is its copies (`xy(?:ab){2}zw` states
# `xyababzw`); W-R1, W-R2, W-R3 and W-R6 are rows S1915, S1916, S1917 and
# S1919's detectors (W-R5's, S1918, is the facts listing).

# W-R4 (span_arms §3.6): T2 row 1 tests the body's MAXIMUM width; `(?:c?){2}` is not width 0, so the run stays `de` (or `ab`); S1906 reads the minimum width, claims `abde` and deletes every match that takes a `c`
pattern ab(?:c?){2}de
features all
m "abcde" 0 5
m "abde" 0 4
m "abccde" 0 6
n "abcccde"
m "xxabcdexx" 2 7
n "abce"

# W-R4 (span_arms §3.6): T2 row 1 tests the body's MAXIMUM width; `(?:c?){2}` is not width 0, so the run stays `de` (or `ab`); S1906 reads the minimum width, claims `abde` and deletes every match that takes a `c` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?:c?){2}de
features all
engine vm
m "abcde" 0 5
m "abde" 0 4
m "abccde" 0 6
n "abcccde"
m "xxabcdexx" 2 7
n "abce"

# W-R1 (span_arms §3.6): `X{m,n}` with m < n is never `all` (T2 row 3), so the run is `xyab` or `abzw`; S1915 sets `all` and claims `xyabzw`, absent from every match that takes two copies
pattern xy(?:ab){1,2}zw
features all
m "xyababzw" 0 8
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabababzw"
n "xyababz"

# W-R1 (span_arms §3.6): `X{m,n}` with m < n is never `all` (T2 row 3), so the run is `xyab` or `abzw`; S1915 sets `all` and claims `xyabzw`, absent from every match that takes two copies [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:ab){1,2}zw
features all
engine vm
m "xyababzw" 0 8
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabababzw"
n "xyababz"

# W-R2 (span_arms §3.6): the power unrolls the copies every match takes (m), never n; S1916 unrolls `rmax` copies and claims `xyababab`, absent from `xyabzw`
pattern xy(?:ab){1,3}zw
features all
m "xyabzw" 0 6
m "xyababzw" 0 8
m "xyabababzw" 0 10
n "xyzw"
n "xyababababzw"

# W-R2 (span_arms §3.6): the power unrolls the copies every match takes (m), never n; S1916 unrolls `rmax` copies and claims `xyababab`, absent from `xyabzw` [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:ab){1,3}zw
features all
engine vm
m "xyabzw" 0 6
m "xyababzw" 0 8
m "xyabababzw" 0 10
n "xyzw"
n "xyababababzw"

# W-R3 (span_arms §3.6): at m = 0 the power has no copy (T2 row 3 at c = 0 is the gap), so the run is `ab` or `ef`; S1917 takes c from max(m, 1) and claims `abcd` or `cdef`, absent from `abef`
pattern ab(?:cd){0,2}ef
features all
m "abef" 0 4
m "abcdef" 0 6
m "abcdcdef" 0 8
n "abcdcdcdef"
n "abcef"

# W-R3 (span_arms §3.6): at m = 0 the power has no copy (T2 row 3 at c = 0 is the gap), so the run is `ab` or `ef`; S1917 takes c from max(m, 1) and claims `abcd` or `cdef`, absent from `abef` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?:cd){0,2}ef
features all
engine vm
m "abef" 0 4
m "abcdef" 0 6
m "abcdcdef" 0 8
n "abcdcdcdef"
n "abcef"

# W-R5 (span_arms §3.6, a FACT witness): `(?:abc){20}` unrolls ceil(32/3) = 11 copies and lists 32 positions, truncated; S1918 stops one copy short (30 positions), sound, so its detector is the facts listing (run_facts_checks.sh [facts-rep]); these cells check the run's answers
pattern (?:abc){20}
features all
m "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc" 0 60
n "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc"
m "xabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc" 1 61
n "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabdabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc"

# W-R5 (span_arms §3.6, a FACT witness): `(?:abc){20}` unrolls ceil(32/3) = 11 copies and lists 32 positions, truncated; S1918 stops one copy short (30 positions), sound, so its detector is the facts listing (run_facts_checks.sh [facts-rep]); these cells check the run's answers [engine vm]
pattern (?:abc){20}
features all
engine vm
m "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc" 0 60
n "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc"
m "xabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc" 1 61
n "abcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabdabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabcabc"

# W-R6 (span_arms §3.6): the width is the repeat's exact one (`rr_rep_w`), never the unrolled copies'; `a.` is not `all`, so 2 copies are unrolled, and S1919 takes their width (4), so the handoff's K is 4 where it is 20 and the attempt at 0 is skipped
pattern (a.){10}xyz
features all
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 0 23
n "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"
m "-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 1 24

# W-R6 (span_arms §3.6): the width is the repeat's exact one (`rr_rep_w`), never the unrolled copies'; `a.` is not `all`, so 2 copies are unrolled, and S1919 takes their width (4), so the handoff's K is 4 where it is 20 and the attempt at 0 is skipped [engine vm]
pattern (a.){10}xyz
features all
engine vm
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 0 23
n "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"
m "-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 1 24

# W-R6's DFA twin (span_arms §3.6): `.?` keeps the run off `dominated`, so K (21) is read; under S1919 it is 5
pattern (?:a.){10}.?xyz
features all
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 0 23
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-qxyz" 0 24
n "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"
ns 2 "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"

# W-R6's DFA twin (span_arms §3.6): `.?` keeps the run off `dominated`, so K (21) is read; under S1919 it is 5 [engine vm]
pattern (?:a.){10}.?xyz
features all
engine vm
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz" 0 23
m "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-qxyz" 0 24
n "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"
ns 2 "a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-a-xyz"

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4): an exact repeat is its copies, the run `xyababzw`
pattern xy(?:ab){2}zw
features all
m "xyababzw" 0 8
n "xyabzw"
n "xyabababzw"
m "--xyababzw--" 2 10

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4): an exact repeat is its copies, the run `xyababzw` [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:ab){2}zw
features all
engine vm
m "xyababzw" 0 8
n "xyabzw"
n "xyabababzw"
m "--xyababzw--" 2 10

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4, r1 F7): `X{0}` is the unit, the run `xyzw`
pattern xy(?:ab){0}zw
features all
m "xyzw" 0 4
n "xyabzw"

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4, r1 F7): `X{0}` is the unit, the run `xyzw` [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:ab){0}zw
features all
engine vm
m "xyzw" 0 4
n "xyabzw"

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4): a cube position in each copy, the run `xa[bc]a[bc]y`
pattern x(?:a[bc]){2}y
features all
m "xabacy" 0 6
m "xacaby" 0 6
n "xabay"
n "xadaby"

# R1 mover (span_arms §3.4): a cube position in each copy, the run `xa[bc]a[bc]y` [engine vm]
pattern x(?:a[bc]){2}y
features all
engine vm
m "xabacy" 0 6
m "xacaby" 0 6
n "xabay"
n "xadaby"

# R1 mover: a variable repeat's tail joins what follows it and its head what precedes it, the run `abcdef` across two repeats
pattern (?:ab){1,2}cd(?:ef){1,2}
features all
m "abcdef" 0 6
m "ababcdefef" 0 10
n "abcef"
n "bcdef"

# R1 mover: a variable repeat's tail joins what follows it and its head what precedes it, the run `abcdef` across two repeats [engine vm]
pattern (?:ab){1,2}cd(?:ef){1,2}
features all
engine vm
m "abcdef" 0 6
m "ababcdefef" 0 10
n "abcef"
n "bcdef"

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, spelled for E1's site): a backreference CONSUMES; `\1*` is not width 0, so the run is `abx`; S1905 tests "carries no run" instead of width 0, sends the backreference to row 1 and claims `abxy`
pattern (ab)x\1*y
features all
m "abxaby" 0 6
m "abxy" 0 4
m "abxababy" 0 8
n "abxa"
n "abxaay"

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, spelled for E1's site): a backreference CONSUMES; `\1*` is not width 0, so the run is `abx`; S1905 tests "carries no run" instead of width 0, sends the backreference to row 1 and claims `abxy` [engine vm]
pattern (ab)x\1*y
features all
engine vm
m "abxaby" 0 6
m "abxy" 0 4
m "abxababy" 0 8
n "abxa"
n "abxaay"

# E-2: a min-0 repeat of an empty group is the unit; the run joins across it (`abcdefgh`)
pattern abcd(?:)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-2: a min-0 repeat of an empty group is the unit; the run joins across it (`abcdefgh`) [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a width-0 assertion (the anchor wrapper's `<anchor EMPTY>` under `*`) is the unit
pattern abcd(?:\b)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a width-0 assertion (the anchor wrapper's `<anchor EMPTY>` under `*`) is the unit [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:\b)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# T2 row 1 at m >= 1: the copies of a width-0 body coincide; this pattern never matches (no boundary between `d` and `e`), and every run is sound for it
pattern abcd(?:\b)+efgh
features all
n "abcdefgh"
n "abcd"
n "efgh"

# T2 row 1 at m >= 1: the copies of a width-0 body coincide; this pattern never matches (no boundary between `d` and `e`), and every run is sound for it [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:\b)+efgh
features all
engine vm
n "abcdefgh"
n "abcd"
n "efgh"

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `*` (`^` lowered to its context node)
pattern abcd(?:^)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcd"
m "xabcdefgh" 1 9

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `*` (`^` lowered to its context node) [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:^)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcd"
m "xabcdefgh" 1 9

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `?`
pattern abcd(?:$)?efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `?` [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:$)?efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a lookahead (its body not read: the run is `xyabzw` through the repeat, never into the body)
pattern xy(?:(?=a))*abzw
features all
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabab"

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a lookahead (its body not read: the run is `xyabzw` through the repeat, never into the body) [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:(?=a))*abzw
features all
engine vm
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabab"

# T2 row 1 at m = n >= 1: three copies of `\B` are one zero-width stretch
pattern ab(?:\B){3}cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"

# T2 row 1 at m = n >= 1: three copies of `\B` are one zero-width stretch [engine vm]
pattern ab(?:\B){3}cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"
